\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ryan\'a0\'a0[10:11 PM]\
[brainstorm] I've been trying to think about how to articulate my take on Routing's current situation and Vince's frustration that surfaced during yesterday's meeting. I don't have a single conclusion and wanted to share my thoughts:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 We have had multiple load balancing exercises to bring in temporary capacity onto Routing over the past 2 quarters. That has only ramped up as ICs (Dev and Emma) have left and the number of support tickets and features bottlenecked by Routing have increased. In combination with Kevin and Magaly, this has probably resulted in undue burden on Vince to onboard individuals.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A secondary exacerbating effect is the dissonance between ICs and leadership (mostly in the past):\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl2\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Tenured(?) ICs: There is significant complexity and gaps in the system that are difficult to understand, especially without fully understanding the system. The push to deliver support tickets (repl scripts to do an action) and client features have exacerbated the problem by forcing action without knowing the system.\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Leadership: There is a capacity gap in Routing, therefore the solution from leadership is piling more ICs onto the team to address the capacity gap.\
\ls1\ilvl2\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9642 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Note: This latest iteration is the first where I have felt significant understanding from leadership that a strong IC without SME does not directly equate to bolstering Routing capacity.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The push to continue addressing support tickets and pushing out client features means that we are intentionally accepting a degraded state of the system. This is both in terms of system functionality and safeguards as well as the integrity of the data. For senior+ engineers who understand the problem, this is problematic.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When going over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/datavant/idsb/pull/38836"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \strokec3 script}} Vince is iterating on yesterday, we both acknowledged that the extent of the problem is worse than either of us had realized.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 There has been dissonance between the push to solve for support burden as the top priority while deprioritizing fixing the system. An example is the reroutes project where the push (before we reset this week) was to automate and remove the engineer from the loop, rather than solving the underlying problems. The impact is that we spend a lot of time educating, speccing for handoff, and talking about the problem rather than addressing the problem.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 There has been a perception (from Product) that Routing is unwilling to accept help from others. My take is that this comes from the pushback (both Vince and I) on onboarding ICs who don't have context and counting that as a "successful mitigation" of capacity problems.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa40\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I am directly working to correct this perception but sharing for awareness.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
